WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.108 --> 00:00:02.068
Consequences deadlier than ever.

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:05.209
The Mafia has gone nuclear.

00:00:45.679 --> 00:00:48.520
A new syndicate has arisen from the shadows of the underworld,

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:51.921
a mafia that is completely different than any other.

00:00:53.003 --> 00:00:57.964
This criminal organization deals in the most dangerous contraband ever to be traded on the black market.

00:00:59.104 --> 00:01:03.606
I'm talking about the radioactive materials used to make nuclear bombs.

00:01:08.223 --> 00:01:10.045
Welcome to the dawn of the nuclear mafia,

00:01:10.685 --> 00:01:13.147
a mutation of established crime organizations.

00:01:13.808 --> 00:01:16.930
Nuclear mafia combines the collaborative efforts of gangsters,

00:01:17.191 --> 00:01:17.751
scientists,

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:19.132
corrupt businessmen,

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:20.634
and government officials.

00:01:22.495 --> 00:01:24.358
Their customers include terrorist groups,

00:01:24.557 --> 00:01:25.538
third world countries,

00:01:25.558 --> 00:01:26.599
and hostile nations.

00:01:29.581 --> 00:01:29.961
In fact,

00:01:30.042 --> 00:01:35.966
anyone with the money and desire for weapons of mass destruction can acquire the services of the nuclear mafia.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:50.185
No other contraband has more value than the elements for the construction of nuclear bombs.

00:01:52.688 --> 00:01:53.569
Pound for pound,

00:01:53.688 --> 00:01:57.813
enriched uranium and plutonium are hundreds of times more expensive than drugs.

00:02:00.676 --> 00:02:04.719
Even material used in warheads and missile systems can be found on the black market.

00:02:05.581 --> 00:02:08.924
The exotic metal beryllium is sold for outrageous sums.

00:02:11.256 --> 00:02:17.359
The black market sale of nuclear material is a major departure from organized crime's normal means of illegal trade.

00:02:21.102 --> 00:02:25.044
Crime bosses used to say that they are in the business of giving the public what it wants.

00:02:27.425 --> 00:02:28.485
When Prohibition hit,

00:02:28.885 --> 00:02:32.027
the mob provided the bootleg booze the American people demanded,

00:02:32.647 --> 00:02:35.308
and an illegal drink was apparently more satisfying.

00:02:36.729 --> 00:02:39.871
Alcohol consumption shot up to record highs during Prohibition.

00:02:40.795 --> 00:02:42.195
The Mafia made a fortune.

00:02:44.037 --> 00:02:46.377
By catering to the public's appetite for gambling,

00:02:46.717 --> 00:02:48.237
the mob hit the jackpot again.

00:02:52.118 --> 00:02:52.780
They were there in the

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:55.280
60s when America's drug culture came of age.

00:02:56.721 --> 00:02:58.180
As flower children got high,

00:02:58.300 --> 00:02:59.621
the Mafia got rich.

00:03:05.082 --> 00:03:07.644
The South American drug barons cashed in the same way.

00:03:09.836 --> 00:03:14.777
Drug kings of Colombia get a cut off nearly every gram of coke sold in North America and Europe.

00:03:15.778 --> 00:03:16.098
In the 70s,

00:03:16.338 --> 00:03:18.038
the godfather of cocaine,

00:03:18.118 --> 00:03:19.080
Pablo Escobar,

00:03:19.539 --> 00:03:21.681
became one of the wealthiest men in the world.

00:03:24.342 --> 00:03:26.962
Asian crime lords forged empires in a similar manner.

00:03:28.524 --> 00:03:32.365
The multitude of opium dens in the Far East backrolled the triads in the early

00:03:33.225 --> 00:03:33.346
1900s.

00:03:34.865 --> 00:03:35.447
Their neighbors,

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:36.007
the Yakuza,

00:03:36.206 --> 00:03:38.408
took advantage of the Japanese love of gambling.

00:03:39.455 --> 00:03:44.138
Now both are global enterprises built on the founding principles of all organized crime,

00:03:44.777 --> 00:03:47.599
providing illegal goods and services to the public.

00:03:54.222 --> 00:03:54.483
Now,

00:03:54.722 --> 00:03:55.643
for the first time,

00:03:56.143 --> 00:04:04.667
a syndicates product is solely for a select group of customers with political agendas and deep pockets and the will to use weapons of mass destruction.

00:04:13.307 --> 00:04:14.788
With organized crime involvement,

00:04:15.509 --> 00:04:19.192
nuclear terrorism could now strike anywhere at any time.

00:04:20.574 --> 00:04:25.137
Many say a nuclear mafia aligned with fanatical and terrorist groups should have been predicted.

00:04:26.438 --> 00:04:26.918
After all,

00:04:27.218 --> 00:04:29.760
no one is more skilled at smuggling than organized crime.

00:04:31.382 --> 00:04:37.046
Moving a pound of uranium past customs is a lot easier than sneaking in 500 tons of cocaine.

00:04:39.709 --> 00:04:42.812
I believe that regardless of the commodity...

00:04:43.456 --> 00:04:47.118
Regardless of the crime that's being committed,

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:52.603
people who want to move goods that are contraband,

00:04:54.365 --> 00:04:55.805
regardless of what that is,

00:04:55.846 --> 00:04:56.427
be it drugs,

00:04:56.466 --> 00:04:58.028
be it nuclear material,

00:04:58.447 --> 00:04:59.909
be it stolen goods,

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:11.959
they'll turn to the organizations that conduct the transportation of those goods around the world and into the country they want it deposited in.

00:05:14.637 --> 00:05:17.104
A decade ago nuclear smuggling was a rare event.

00:05:17.644 --> 00:05:18.245
No longer.

00:05:19.225 --> 00:05:23.009
Many experts conclude the demand for nuclear weapons must be greater than ever.

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:24.390
Recently,

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:27.833
there has been a major increase in the trafficking of nuclear material.

00:05:32.216 --> 00:05:37.001
...are holding two individuals for attempting to sell stolen radioactive material.

00:05:37.261 --> 00:05:41.344
The two had in their possessions 82 kilograms of radioactive material,

00:05:41.705 --> 00:05:43.386
including enriched uranium.

00:05:43.486 --> 00:05:45.508
Lithuanian officials have determined...

00:05:45.972 --> 00:05:51.636
The 100 kilograms of radioactive material seized last month from an armed gang is uranium.

00:05:51.756 --> 00:06:00.482
The German Parliamentary Commission investigating a plutonium smuggling incident has learned that smugglers offered to supply 11 kilograms of Russian-origin...

00:06:00.722 --> 00:06:04.266
weapons-grade plutonium enough to build three nuclear missiles.

00:06:04.867 --> 00:06:06.709
According to Italian press reports,

00:06:06.949 --> 00:06:15.620
Italian prosecutors have arrested a man with links to the United States Central Intelligence Agency and an Italian-American mafia as part of their investigation.

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:17.562
of smuggling radioactive materials...

00:06:17.582 --> 00:06:20.564
During a search of a car at the Polish-Czech border,

00:06:20.904 --> 00:06:25.728
Polish border guards discovered 11 cigarette-pack-sized containers filled with strontium-90.

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:32.754
Bulgarian police have broken an international smuggling ring involving Russians and Ukrainians.

00:06:32.755 --> 00:06:33.775
This just in for Munich.

00:06:34.015 --> 00:06:37.758
Highly radioactive plutonium was found on board a commercial flight from Moscow.

00:06:38.118 --> 00:06:41.841
German SWAT teams apprehended the smugglers before the deadly cargo could be sold.

00:06:42.281 --> 00:06:42.742
Reportedly,

00:06:42.802 --> 00:06:45.504
the black market price of the 4 kilograms of plutonium...

00:06:45.764 --> 00:06:49.185
needed to build a nuclear bomb is $350 million.

00:06:51.486 --> 00:06:51.606
See,

00:06:51.607 --> 00:06:58.868
it doesn't make any difference if the kilogram of plutonium that shows up in a terrorist device comes from China or from Russia or from Kazakhstan.

00:06:59.429 --> 00:07:00.029
If it shows up,

00:07:00.049 --> 00:07:00.749
it's bad news.

00:07:05.611 --> 00:07:08.732
There have been hundreds of attempts to steal nuclear materials in Russia.

00:07:15.928 --> 00:07:20.370
Often the thefts can be traced to workers employed at nuclear facilities or research centers.

00:07:26.312 --> 00:07:29.993
Even live nuclear warheads have gone missing from weapons assembly plants.

00:07:31.674 --> 00:07:35.235
The stolen nuclear goods can then be fenced to organize crime.

00:07:39.052 --> 00:07:40.013
In the late 90s,

00:07:40.433 --> 00:07:48.097
the secret workings of the nuclear mafia first came to the surface with the discovery of a smuggling operation that was being run through a seaport in Lithuania.

00:07:49.218 --> 00:07:52.740
It started out as just a routine investigation by a tough cop.

00:07:59.744 --> 00:08:02.045
The case file read like the usual gang war,

00:08:02.765 --> 00:08:04.787
but to Detective Joseph Rimcovicious,

00:08:05.007 --> 00:08:07.268
the violence and killings just didn't add up.

00:08:09.748 --> 00:08:11.029
The port of Klaipeda,

00:08:11.710 --> 00:08:13.952
Lithuania's gateway to the world.

00:08:15.233 --> 00:08:15.954
Unfortunately,

00:08:16.054 --> 00:08:19.457
it has also become the crossroads for smugglers of all kinds.

00:08:21.439 --> 00:08:23.200
My caseload is the usual.

00:08:23.821 --> 00:08:24.642
Drug running,

00:08:24.882 --> 00:08:25.863
black market liquor,

00:08:25.983 --> 00:08:26.864
cigarette smuggling.

00:08:28.285 --> 00:08:29.286
But this case...

00:08:30.587 --> 00:08:31.828
Contract killings,

00:08:31.968 --> 00:08:32.929
bombed vehicles,

00:08:33.009 --> 00:08:33.630
shootouts...

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:35.391
It didn't make sense.

00:08:38.992 --> 00:08:40.714
But then I got the break I needed.

00:08:41.614 --> 00:08:43.997
I didn't know it was from a dead woman.

00:08:46.519 --> 00:08:47.800
They said to give you this.

00:08:52.244 --> 00:08:53.585
Not again.

00:08:54.326 --> 00:08:56.207
Lola Person's got to earn a living.

00:08:56.948 --> 00:08:58.009
In the new Lithuania,

00:08:58.309 --> 00:08:59.750
