00:14:19.336 --> 00:14:21.817
A businessman I know from Sverdlovsk.

00:14:22.537 --> 00:14:23.838
He now lives in Moscow.

00:14:26.119 --> 00:14:27.059
Boris Dimitriev.

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:30.281
Where did he get his money?

00:14:31.703 --> 00:14:35.447
His money?

00:14:35.587 --> 00:14:36.327
I'm a scientist,

00:14:36.347 --> 00:14:36.808
I don't know.

00:14:37.449 --> 00:14:38.249
Karate clubs.

00:14:39.691 --> 00:14:40.792
Karate clubs,

00:14:40.872 --> 00:14:41.413
my ass.

00:14:47.279 --> 00:14:51.863
That gentleman operates in the grey zone between the legal world and the underworld.

00:14:52.960 --> 00:14:58.363
One way that Russian organized crime makes money is through the buying and selling of commodities.

00:14:59.244 --> 00:15:00.645
Buy the materials in rubles,

00:15:00.885 --> 00:15:02.526
sell them outside the country for dollars.

00:15:03.367 --> 00:15:04.747
For a businessman like him,

00:15:05.188 --> 00:15:07.029
this was an easy way to make a fortune.

00:15:08.890 --> 00:15:17.896
His rise to wealth and power began when he defied the communists and opened a string of video shops that were outlets for black market pornography smuggled from Europe and America.

00:15:18.912 --> 00:15:25.195
He emerged after the fall of communism as one of the new breed of Soviet businessmen who worked both sides of the law.

00:15:26.095 --> 00:15:26.556
In the early

00:15:26.996 --> 00:15:29.117
90s, he opened up a chain of karate clubs.

00:15:29.617 --> 00:15:37.521
These so-called sports clubs are actually training grounds for thugs hired as security to protect mafia bosses.

00:15:38.745 --> 00:15:45.128
I told Dmitriyev that I knew a man in Switzerland who knew a man in North Korea who's willing to buy beryllium for 24 million dollars,

00:15:45.608 --> 00:15:48.329
but he had to supply the muscle and the financing for it.

00:15:48.349 --> 00:15:48.809
Very simple.

00:15:48.869 --> 00:15:49.329
Case closed.

00:15:49.330 --> 00:15:49.670
Can I go?

00:15:51.570 --> 00:15:54.471
Yeah.

00:15:54.472 --> 00:15:55.072
One more time.

00:15:56.212 --> 00:15:56.332
So,

00:15:56.652 --> 00:16:01.154
Igor arranged for Dmitriyev's men to smuggle the beryllium to Switzerland by way of Lithuania.

00:16:01.155 --> 00:16:02.055
I tell you,

00:16:02.395 --> 00:16:03.795
I did nothing illegal.

00:16:03.815 --> 00:16:07.597
The Russian authorities never arrested anyone for smuggling radioactive materials.

00:16:10.597 --> 00:16:11.958
We seized the beryllium,

00:16:12.238 --> 00:16:13.859
but couldn't arrest anyone.

00:16:15.159 --> 00:16:17.821
What's illegal in one country is obviously illegal in another.

00:16:19.042 --> 00:16:21.503
As long as the present laws remain on the books,

00:16:23.144 --> 00:16:25.905
and corruption plagues the officials running these facilities,

00:16:26.586 --> 00:16:31.468
the nuclear mafia will always have the upper hand.

00:16:38.332 --> 00:16:40.113
The beryllium was bound for North Korea.

00:16:41.233 --> 00:16:45.795
It is believed the mafia was tracking that nation's attempt to develop nuclear weapons for years.

00:16:46.856 --> 00:16:50.717
Now with widespread corruption in Russia and the reduction of their nuclear security,

00:16:51.758 --> 00:16:56.520
many conclude it won't be long before North Korea possesses a nuclear arsenal.

00:17:04.183 --> 00:17:07.945
The Soviet Union that was once called the evil empire is long dead.

00:17:08.873 --> 00:17:12.515
The systems that once prevented the theft of nuclear weapons died with it.

00:17:15.737 --> 00:17:16.958
The Cold War is over.

00:17:17.158 --> 00:17:19.079
Nuclear weapons development has diminished,

00:17:19.880 --> 00:17:21.200
but the stockpiles remain.

00:17:22.921 --> 00:17:26.924
With an underworld organization specializing in the theft of nuclear materials,

00:17:27.184 --> 00:17:32.767
the prospect of nuclear devastation is greater now than at any time in the history of nuclear arms,

00:17:33.108 --> 00:17:35.189
which began over five decades ago.

00:17:37.165 --> 00:17:38.987
In August of 1945,

00:17:38.988 --> 00:17:43.571
the atom was cracked and a horrible new weapon brought World War II to a swift and decisive end.

00:17:51.658 --> 00:17:53.080
Harness for ground warfare.

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:57.043
New chapter incidents have been written in the now familiar towering,

00:17:57.123 --> 00:17:57.484
billowing,

00:17:57.504 --> 00:17:59.185
and sinister mushroom cloud.

00:17:59.646 --> 00:18:01.307
Trademark of the atomic explosion.

00:18:01.387 --> 00:18:03.049
But the nuclear genie was out.

00:18:05.725 --> 00:18:07.226
Soon the arms race was on.

00:18:11.970 --> 00:18:13.351
Throughout the next three decades,

00:18:13.371 --> 00:18:17.114
the weapons labs in the Soviet Union and the United States were going full tilt.

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:28.944
Many feared the two superpowers racing to see who could blow up the world the most times.

00:18:32.249 --> 00:18:36.713
This is the terror that once again casts its eerie shadow over the face of the earth.

00:18:37.293 --> 00:18:41.276
The hydrogen bomb.

00:18:41.277 --> 00:18:42.537
At the height of the Cold War,

00:18:42.918 --> 00:18:47.902
the combined arsenal of the two superpowers was over 100,000 nuclear warheads.

00:18:48.842 --> 00:18:51.024
The entire world lived on the edge of an abyss.

00:18:54.065 --> 00:18:57.227
It was predicted the ash from a nuclear war would blot out the sun,

00:18:58.268 --> 00:19:00.109
nuclear winter would descend on the world,

00:19:00.930 --> 00:19:01.571
and a final,

00:19:01.711 --> 00:19:02.131
lifeless,

00:19:02.271 --> 00:19:03.572
dark age would begin.

00:19:07.315 --> 00:19:08.836
With the fall of the Soviet Union,

00:19:08.856 --> 00:19:11.178
the world stepped back from the brink of a nuclear war.

00:19:12.258 --> 00:19:14.760
But the threat from nuclear weapons is worse than ever.

00:19:18.541 --> 00:19:23.882
Decades of testing and research have unraveled the complexities of nuclear bomb construction.

